# SABOTAGE: WS-NOTES Phase 3 unit 3.12 — THE BULK EMPTY EMPTIES ONE PAGE AND REPORTS SUCCESS
# "Empty the trash" is the same governed write applied to EVERY page the trash holds, inside one
# transaction. This patch keeps only the first row it found (`Enum.take(1)`) — the shape of a
# "the loop is slow, just take one" change — so the button reports "1 page deleted permanently"
# while the rest of the trash is still there, and nothing in the audit trail says a page the user
# asked to destroy was kept.
#
# Silent everywhere else: the per-page guard, the cascade, the audit and the transaction are
# untouched; the survivor set is simply never read. Only the "every trashed page" assertion
# distinguishes an empty from a one-page delete.
#
# Aimed at the SET the bulk write acts on. The single-page purge is untouched.
#
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/notes_trash_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: an admin empties EVERY trashed page in one write
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/notes/writes.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/notes/writes.ex
@@ -793,6 +793,7 @@
         # pass from asking for a page the first one destroyed (which would be `:not_found` and would
         # roll the whole empty back for no reason).
         docs
+        |> Enum.take(1)
         |> Enum.reduce_while({:ok, [], MapSet.new()}, fn doc, {:ok, acc, done} ->
           if MapSet.member?(done, doc.id) do
             {:cont, {:ok, acc, done}}
